- What data would you surface in dashboards to operators during a flash spike?

## Concept Overview
OpenTelemetry provides a unified approach to observability by collecting metrics, traces, and logs. For SRE, RED metrics (Rate, Errors, Duration) are essential for monitoring service health.

## Implementation Details
- Use OpenTelemetry SDK with Prometheus exporter
- Instrument HTTP endpoints using middleware
- Create custom metrics for request counting and error tracking
- Configure latency histograms with appropriate buckets

## Code Example
```javascript
const { NodeSDK } = require('@opentelemetry/sdk-node');
const { PrometheusExporter } = require('@opentelemetry/exporter-prometheus');
const { metrics } = require('@opentelemetry/api');

const exporter = new PrometheusExporter({ port: 9464 });
const sdk = new NodeSDK({ metricExporter: exporter });

// Create RED metrics
const meter = metrics.getMeter('service-metrics');
const requestCounter = meter.createCounter('http_requests_total');
const errorCounter = meter.createCounter('http_errors_total');
const durationHistogram = meter.createHistogram('http_request_duration_ms');
```

## Common Pitfalls
- Incorrect bucket configuration leading to poor latency visibility
- Missing error classification for different HTTP status codes
- High cardinality metrics from excessive label usage
- Not sampling traces appropriately in high-traffic scenarios

## Why This Is Asked

Assesss real-world ability to design resilient, low-tail-latency multi-region pipelines under stress while preserving tenant fairness and clear rollback paths.

## Key Concepts

- Backpressure and circuit breaking in streaming pipelines
- Per-tenant QoS and traffic shaping
- Exactly-once processing guarantees across Kafka and sinks
- Observability for SLO-driven tail latency
- Chaos testing and incident rollback discipline

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: bounded per-tenant backpressure
function handleEvent(event, tenant) {
  const q = queues[tenant];
  if (q.length < MAX_PER_TENANT) {
    enqueue(event, tenant);
  } else {
    drop(event); // apply backpressure upstream
  }
}
```

